    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Lucan's leading estate agents take great pleasure in presenting 26 Mount Andrew Court, a lovely two bedroom terraced home which is presented in pristine condition throughout. This light filled home boasts a fantastic location within St Mary's Parish and offers a small private garden to the rear with gated pedestrian access, while to the front ample resident parking is available.\n\nMeasuring 65 sq.m/700 sq.ft of beautifully presented interiors, 26 Mount Andrew Court offers a turnkey opportunity for the discerning purchasers. With benefits including a modern fitted kitchen, modern fitted fully tiled bathroom suite, gas fired central heating with a new gas boiler and double-glazed windows.\n\nMount Andrew is an exceptional, low-density, residential development, set on meticulously maintained grounds & gardens, ideally located on the periphery of Lucan village, just off the N4. There is ample, free residents parking. The property is located only a short walk from both Hermitage Park and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre.\n\nAn abundance of essential and recreational amenities can also be enjoyed with great ease. Within close proximity to the M4/M50/M7, QBC, Nitelink, Adamstown Train Station, Liffey Valley & Ballyowen shopping centres, as well as a host of other amenities that include a variety schools, public transport, parks and sporting facilities. Other local recreational amenities of note include Vesey Park, Hermitage Park, St. Catherine's Park, Westmanstown Sports Centre and Hermitage & Lucan Golf Club. Mount Andrew is readily accessible to Intel, Hewlett Packard, Grangecastle and the wider area around Castleknock, Pheonix Park & Blanchardstown.\n\nProviding an ideal opportunity for first time buyers and investors alike, viewing comes highly recommended. 3D Virtual Tour available online and physical viewing by appointment, please phone selling agents DNG on 01-6280400."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - .9m x .75m\nWelcoming entrance with wood flooring and alarm panel\n\nLiving Room - 3.75m x 4.42m\nSpacious living room to the front with wood flooring, an open fireplace, tv point, ceiling centre rose and ceiling coving\n\nKitchen - 3.76m x 3.25m\nModern fitted kitchen to the rear with fitted wall and floor units, tiled flooring, under stair storage space and sliding glass doors to the garden\n\nLanding - .98m x 2.14m\nWith attic access and carpeted flooring\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.75m x 3.22m\nSpacious double bedroom to the rear with wood flooring, built in wardrobes and tv point\n\nBathroom - 2.75m x 1.5m\nFully tiled bathroom with a bath, triton shower, chrome towel rail, wc and whb\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.75m x 2.62m\nLarge double bedroom to the front with built in wardrobes and wood flooring\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 2 Bedroom home</li><li> Pristine condition throughout</li><li> Small private garden</li><li> Gated pedestrian access to the rear</li><li> Ample residents parking space to the front</li><li> Modern fitted kitchen</li><li> Modern fully tiled bathroom</li><li> Ideal for 1st time buyers and investors alike</li><li> Recently installed new gas boiler</li><li> Double glazed windows</li><li> Owner occupied</li><li> Built c.2002</li><li> Mang fee: 582 per annum</li><li> Within close proximity of a host of amenities</li><li> Easy access to the city & M50</li><li> Short stroll to Liffey Valley Shopping Centre</li><li> Sought after development</li><li> St Mary's Parish</li><li> Well serviced by public transport links</ul>"
      },
